# Yoink AI Assistant Rules

## Environment Setup
- Always run the application in a Python virtual environment
- Create virtual environment using: `python -m venv .venv`
- Activate virtual environment before running.
- Install development dependencies in virtual environment: `pip install -r requirements-dev.txt`
- Never run the application without activating the virtual environment

## Code Style
- Follow PEP 8 guidelines for Python code
- Use type hints where possible
- Keep functions focused and single-purpose
- Document all public functions and classes

## Project Structure
- Keep the PyQt shell in flat modules such as `main.py`, `main_window.py`, and `bridge.py`
- Database operations live in `db.py` and `models.py`
- Core torrent functionality lives in `src/torrents/`
- Utility functions live in `src/utils/`

## Testing
- Write unit tests for core functionality
- Test GUI components separately
- Include error handling tests

## Documentation
- Keep README.md up to date
- Document all API changes
- Include examples for common operations

## Security
- Never expose API keys in code
- Validate all user inputs
- Handle file paths securely

## Performance
- Use async operations for network calls
- Optimize database queries
- Cache frequently accessed data

## Error Handling
- Log all errors with appropriate context
- Provide user-friendly error messages
- Handle network errors gracefully 